## Generated for each parsed OPC UA TCP message or reassembled message.
##
## This event is generated for Hello/Acknowledge messages, secure-channel
## messages, and service messages decoded from one or more message chunks.
##
## c: The connection.
##
## is_orig: True if the message originated at the TCP originator.
##
## message_type: OPC UA transport message type (``HEL``, ``ACK``, ``OPN``,
##               ``MSG``, ``CLO``, or ``ABO``).
##
## service: The decoded service name, or ``Encrypted``/``Unknown`` when body
##          decoding is not possible.
##
## endpoint: The most recently observed endpoint URL on the connection.
##
## security_policy: The most recently observed OPC UA security policy URI.
##
## security_mode: The negotiated security mode (``None``, ``Sign``, or
##                ``SignAndEncrypt``).
##
## status: StatusCode value from the response. For service responses with
##         per-operation results, this is the first non-Good result, if any.
##
## has_status: True if *status* was present in the message.
##
## session_id: The NodeId of the most recently observed session.
##
## subscription_id: The most recently observed subscription identifier.
##
## has_subscription: True if *subscription_id* applies to this message.
##
## request_id: The secure-channel request identifier.
##
## chunk_type: ``C`` for a continuation chunk or ``F`` for a final chunk.
##
## chunk_count: Number of chunks used for this message.
##
## message_size: Size of the final transport chunk, including its message
##               header, or the reassembled chunk payload size.
##
## node_ids: NodeIds retained from the service request.
##
## extension_objects: ExtensionObject type NodeIds observed in the message.
event opcua_message%(c: connection, is_orig: bool, message_type: string, service: string,
                     endpoint: string, security_policy: string, security_mode: string,
                     status: count, has_status: bool, session_id: string,
                     subscription_id: count, has_subscription: bool, request_id: count,
                     chunk_type: string, chunk_count: count, message_size: count,
                     node_ids: string_vec, extension_objects: string_vec%);
